         <h3>Cardona-gram, a word game</h3>
         <div class="meta"><span><b>Team</b> Ana Isabel Cardona, Leonardo Di Tommaso, Tim Langenbahn</span></div>
-        <p>A Python anagram game: the player gets a random set of letters and has to find every English word hidden in it. It has a classic mode, a survival mode with three lives, and a 60-second timed mode. This was one of my first coding projects, written without generative AI.</p>
+        <p>A Python anagram game: the player gets a random set of letters and has to find every English word hidden in it. It has a classic mode, a survival mode with three lives, and a 60-second timed mode. My part was the word engine, and it taught me to pick a simple data structure over a clever dependency when speed and reliability matter more.</p>
         <p>I built the word engine: generating every permutation of three or more letters and checking which ones are real words. We tried an online dictionary API, an offline spell-check library and a CSV of about 4,000 common words. We chose the CSV because it was faster, needed no extra dependencies and produced words players actually know, at the cost of missing rarer words.</p>
